  "findings": [
    "Removing only lane produces identical resolved hashes for all 180 functions.",
    "Removing only offset changes only VCL, increasing its materialized differing-byte count from 784 to 923 and moving first raw divergence from 562 to 3. No exact function is gained.",
    "The baseline first raw divergence at offset 562 is a branch displacement. The first changed instruction placement is at offset 641: candidate reloads high from [esp+1Ch] before the output branch, where original reloads separately at offsets 647 and 659. The fourth lane has the same duplication/hoist distinction.",
    "Later differences are low/high shift and OR scheduling plus selector register choice in lanes three/four. The target RET is at offset 1464; candidate RET is at 1456. Both occupied extents are 1472 bytes; equal extent does not prove matching body.",
    "All 168 exact baseline functions, 179 other function hashes and all 25 objects/11 fields remain unchanged. No source promotion or new behavioral claim."
  ],
